# bob (ai, seat 1) is the active player with Boggart Brute (3/2, menace)
# already attacking alice (human, seat 0) directly; alice holds two Walls of
# Stone (0/8), either of which may block it, and both of which must for the
# block to be legal. Landed at Declare ATTACKERS Step, for the reason
# `w54-b-two-blockers.state` gives: the attacker's own priority stop there is
# driven through the ordinary main loop, so state effects have run before
# Forge decides who may block.
#
# Walls, not 1/1s: the double block deals the Brute's 3 damage to an 0/8 wall
# and none back, so every creature is still on the board at Combat Damage,
# where the declared block is read. Unblocked, the Brute's 3 reach alice.
turn=1
activeplayer=ai
activephase=COMBAT_DECLARE_ATTACKERS
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=
humanbattlefield=Wall of Stone;Wall of Stone
humanlibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
humangraveyard=
aihand=
aibattlefield=Boggart Brute|Attacking
ailibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
aigraveyard=
